/den
/staging/
# `.claude/` is also excluded by .git/info/exclude, which is local and reaches no clone.
# .gitignore outranks info/exclude, so this line is what lets git descend at all — without
# it the negations below are never even evaluated, because git does not walk into an
# excluded directory. The contents stay ignored by the pattern that follows.
!.claude/
.claude/**
.superpowers
!.claude/settings.json
# The slash commands are project tooling, not local state: they must reach a clone. The
# directory needs its own negation for the same descend reason as above.
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/commands/*.md
/dist/
# Agent scratch notes: measurements and analyses written during a session, kept LOCAL on
# purpose. They are dated primary sources for the machine they were measured on, not project
# documentation — what a note proves and the project keeps belongs in `docs/superpowers/`.
/claudedocs/
